triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.PlayAnimation.Animation.tooltip = Animation set key to play (model-specific, e.g. Eat or Idle). Works both ways with Apply On: pick a target first and this list only shows animations its model has. Pick an animation first and the Apply On list only shows targets that can play it. If the two no longer match, the mismatched one is flagged (unsupported). Looping ones are marked and need a Duration or a Stop effect to end.
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.PlayAnimation.Slot.tooltip = Animation layer to play in. Layers are independent and higher layers override lower ones per bone, so an animation here plays on top of (or under) whatever else the entity is doing.
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.PlayAnimation.Target.tooltip = Which entities animate. Entities In Volume searches everything inside the volume regardless of the volume's Target Types and always includes the triggering entity, even if it has already left (On Exit or delayed effects). Narrow it with Apply On. Triggering Entity animates only the entity that set the volume off.
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.PlayAnimation.NpcType.tooltip = Optional filter for who is animated: a specific NPC role, Player (players only), or Everyone (NPCs and players). Works both ways with Animation: set a target and the Animation picker only lists what its model can play. Set an animation first and this picker only lists targets that have it. If the two no longer match, the mismatched one is flagged (unsupported). Leave empty to animate every NPC inside.
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.PlayAnimation.Duration.tooltip = Seconds to play before the animation is cleared. 0 plays normally (looping animations run forever). The timer fires even after the entity leaves the volume.
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.PlayAnimation.Stop.tooltip = When on, clears the chosen Slot instead of playing. Pair an On Exit effect with Stop to cancel a looping animation when the entity leaves the volume.
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.PlayAnimation.Slot.option.Movement = Movement
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.PlayAnimation.Slot.option.Status = Status
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.PlayAnimation.Slot.option.Action = Action
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.PlayAnimation.Slot.option.Face = Face
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.PlayAnimation.Slot.option.Emote = Emote
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.PlayAnimation.Slot.option.Movement.tooltip = Locomotion layer (walk/run/idle). Overwritten every tick by the movement system, so animations placed here are stomped almost immediately. Avoid.
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.PlayAnimation.Slot.option.Status.tooltip = Ongoing-state layer above locomotion: sleeping, alerted, eating. Good for looping animations that should survive while the entity keeps moving.
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.PlayAnimation.Slot.option.Action.tooltip = One-shot action layer. On players this plays above their own item and attack animations without interrupting them. Skips the model-support check, so unsupported keys fail silently here.
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.PlayAnimation.Slot.option.Face.tooltip = Facial bones only, for expressions. Full-body animations placed here will appear to do nothing.
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.PlayAnimation.Slot.option.Emote.tooltip = Topmost layer, overrides everything else. Best choice for forced full-body animations like dances. Clearing it returns the entity to whatever the lower layers were doing.
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.PlayAnimation.Target.option.TRIGGERING_ENTITY = Triggering Entity
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.PlayAnimation.Target.option.TRIGGERING_ENTITY.tooltip = Only the entity that set the volume off, if it matches Apply On.
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.PlayAnimation.Target.option.NPCS_IN_VOLUME = Entities In Volume
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.PlayAnimation.Target.option.NPCS_IN_VOLUME.tooltip = Everything matching Apply On that is inside the volume when the effect fires, plus the triggering entity even if it has already left.
