triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.ReplaceBlockType.ToBlockState = To Block State
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.ReplaceBlockType.Origin = Origin
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.Teleport.RelativeToVolume.tooltip = Add Position as an offset from the trigger volume's origin instead of using Position as an absolute destination.
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.PlaySound.Location.tooltip = Where the sound originates. Volume Center and Entity are spatial (3D) and limited by the sound asset's max distance. Player is non-spatial (2D) and always audible to the triggering player.
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.PlaySound.Offset.tooltip = Position offset added to the chosen 3D origin. Ignored for Player.
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.PlaySound.Location.option.VOLUME_CENTER = Volume Center
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.PlaySound.Location.option.ENTITY = Entity
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.PlaySound.Location.option.EVENT = Event / Signal
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.PlaySound.Location.option.PLAYER = Player
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.PlaySound.Location.option.VOLUME_CENTER.tooltip = Play 3D at the volume center.
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.PlaySound.Location.option.ENTITY.tooltip = Play 3D at the triggering entity's position.
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.PlaySound.Location.option.EVENT.tooltip = Play 3D at the position the triggering event happened, or the origin carried by a received signal.
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.PlaySound.Location.option.PLAYER.tooltip = Play non-spatial 2D to the triggering player only, audible regardless of distance.
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.TimeOfDay.MinHour.tooltip = Start of the hour-of-day window (0 to 24). When the start hour is later than the end hour the window spans midnight, e.g. 18 to 6 covers dusk through dawn.
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.TimeOfDay.MaxHour.tooltip = End of the hour-of-day window (0 to 24). When the start hour is later than the end hour the window spans midnight, e.g. 18 to 6 covers dusk through dawn.
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.TagCondition.Comparison.tooltip = How the tag's value is compared against Tag Value. Exactly and Not Equal compare the text, and Not Equal still requires the tag key to be present. At Least, At Most, More Than and Less Than treat both values as numbers and never pass when either one is not a number.
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.TagCondition.Inverted.tooltip = Off (default): passes when the tag is present. On: inverts the check so it passes when the tag is absent.
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.BlockTypeCondition.State.tooltip = Match only when the block's state is one of these variants (e.g. Off, On, OpenDoorIn). Separate multiple states with commas to match any of them. Use default for the base state. Leave empty to match any state. Reads the live world block, so on a block-used event it reflects the state after the interaction. Press F7 in-game to inspect the state of the block you're looking at.
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.PlayVfx.Anchor.tooltip = Where the particle spawns: the volume center, the triggering entity, or the position the event/signal happened at.
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.PlayVfx.Anchor.option.VOLUME.tooltip = Spawn at the volume center plus Offset.
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.PlayVfx.Anchor.option.ENTITY.tooltip = Spawn at the triggering entity position plus Offset.
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.PlayVfx.Anchor.option.EVENT.tooltip = Spawn at the position the triggering event happened (a block event's block, otherwise the actor), or the origin carried by a received signal.
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.PastePrefab.Origin.tooltip = How Position is interpreted: an offset from the volume origin, the triggering entity, or where the event/signal happened, or an absolute world coordinate.
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.PastePrefab.Origin.option.VOLUME_ORIGIN.tooltip = Add Position to the trigger volume origin.
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.PastePrefab.Origin.option.ENTITY.tooltip = Add Position to the triggering entity position.
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.PastePrefab.Origin.option.EVENT.tooltip = Add Position to where the triggering event happened, or the origin carried by a received signal.
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.PastePrefab.Origin.option.WORLD_ABSOLUTE.tooltip = Treat Position as an absolute world coordinate.
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.PastePrefab.Rotation.tooltip = Yaw rotation applied to the pasted prefab. A trigger volume rotated on paste adds its rotation to this value.
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.RemoveEntities.Mode.tooltip = Kill runs the normal lethal-damage path (death animation and loot). Remove despawns entities silently. Players are never removed under Remove; use Kill to affect players.
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.RemoveEntities.IncludeNpcs.tooltip = Affect NPCs inside the volume. Narrow to specific roles with NPC Roles.
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.RemoveEntities.IncludePlayers.tooltip = Affect players inside the volume. Players are only removed by Kill. Remove skips them.
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.RemoveEntities.IgnoreInvulnerability.tooltip = Kill even invulnerable targets, including creative-mode players (like the /kill command). Off by default so builders in creative aren't killed while testing.
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.RemoveEntities.Roles.tooltip = NPC roles to affect. Leave empty to affect every NPC inside the volume.
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.RemoveEntities.MaxCount.tooltip = Maximum number of entities affected per activation. 0 removes or kills all of them.
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.NoTick.ScheduledTick.tooltip = Stop scheduled growth ticks inside the volume (crops and other timed plant growth). Growth resumes when the volume is removed or disabled.
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.NoTick.RandomTick.tooltip = Stop random ticks inside the volume (grass spread and other random block updates). Resumes when the volume is removed or disabled.
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.CancelParticles.ParticleSystems.tooltip = Particle systems to cancel. Leave empty to cancel any type. Only affects systems still playing that started inside the volume. It cannot stop systems that already finished or ambient effects the client spawns on its own.
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.CancelParticles.Instant.tooltip = On removes the particles immediately. Off lets them fade out naturally.
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.RunRootInteraction.EquipSlot = Equip Slot
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.RunRootInteraction.EquipSlot.tooltip = Armor slot index used only when Interaction Type is Equipped (0 = first armor slot).
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.common.ExceptBlocks.tooltip = Block types this rule does not apply to, as comma-separated block ids. Leave empty for no exceptions.
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.NoBuild.ExceptBlocks.tooltip = Block types placement is allowed for, as comma-separated block ids. Filter blocks (reference blocks that stand for a whole family) are allowed and expand to their member blocks. Leave empty for no exceptions.
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.NoUse.ExceptBlocks.tooltip = Block ids that stay usable, as comma-separated ids. Also matches pickupable block/item entities placed with the entity tool by their item id. Filter blocks (reference blocks that stand for a whole family) are allowed and expand to their member blocks. Leave empty for no exceptions.
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.common.ExceptBlockTags.tooltip = Block tags this rule does not apply to, as comma-separated tag names. Any block carrying one of these tags is excepted.
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.common.ExceptTools.tooltip = Held items that bypass this rule, as comma-separated item ids. Leave empty for no exceptions.
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.common.ExceptToolTags.tooltip = Item tags that bypass this rule, as comma-separated tag names. Any held item carrying one of these tags is excepted.
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.common.Target.tooltip = Who receives the reject signal when this rule blocks an action. Self signals this rule's own volume, Other signals volumes matched by Match Tag Key within Radius of the blocked block, and Both does both. The signal carries the blocked block's position.
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.common.SignalKeys.tooltip = Comma-separated tag keys the reject signal carries when this rule blocks an action. Receivers match them with a Tag Condition (Source: Event / Signal), and the signal also carries the blocked block's position so effects fire at the denied spot. Paired by position with Reject Signal Values.
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.common.SignalValues.tooltip = Optional comma-separated value for each Reject Signal Key, paired by position. A receiving Tag Condition matches a key only when its Tag Value also matches (blank matches any). Leave an entry blank to send that key with no value.
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.common.EntityFilter.tooltip = Which entities this rule applies to: all entities, all except those listed in Entities, or only those listed.
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.common.Entities.tooltip = Comma-separated NPC role names (e.g. Trork_Warrior). Use Player to match players. Used by the All Except Listed and Only Listed entity filters.
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.NoDamage.PvpOnly.tooltip = When on, only damage dealt by another player is cancelled, so PvE damage still applies.
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.common.EntityFilter.option.ALL = All
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.common.EntityFilter.option.EXCEPT = All Except Listed
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.common.EntityFilter.option.ONLY = Only Listed
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.DamageMultiplier.Multiplier.tooltip = Damage is multiplied by this value. Above 1 increases damage, below 1 reduces it, 0 negates it.
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.DamageMultiplier.Direction.tooltip = Entity Filter / Entities pick the affected entity. The other party in the hit is not filtered. Received multiplies the damage that entity takes, so it is the victim and the attacker can be anyone. Dealt multiplies the damage that entity deals, so it is the attacker and the victim can be anyone. Both applies when the affected entity is on either side. With Entity Filter set to All, every entity in the volume is affected.
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.DamageMultiplier.Direction.option.RECEIVED = Received (affected entity is the victim)
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.DamageMultiplier.Direction.option.DEALT = Dealt (affected entity is the attacker)
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.DamageMultiplier.Direction.option.BOTH = Both (affected entity on either side)
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.DamageMultiplier.EntityFilter.tooltip = Picks the affected entity that Apply To refers to: the victim for Received, the attacker for Dealt, or either side for Both. The other party in the hit is not filtered. All affects every entity in the volume. Only Listed and All Except Listed narrow it to the Entities below.
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.DamageMultiplier.Entities.tooltip = Comma-separated NPC role names (e.g. Skeleton_Archer). Use Player for players. These are the affected entities for Only Listed and All Except Listed, and are ignored when Entity Filter is All.
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.NoBuild.ExceptBlocks.placeholder = e.g. Dirt, Stone
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.NoBuild.ExceptBlockTags.placeholder = e.g. Soil
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.NoDestroy.ExceptBlocks.placeholder = e.g. Dirt, Stone
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.NoDestroy.ExceptBlockTags.placeholder = e.g. Soil
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.NoDestroy.ExceptTools.placeholder = e.g. Tool_Pickaxe_Iron
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.NoDestroy.ExceptToolTags.placeholder = e.g. Pickaxe
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.NoHarvest.ExceptBlocks.placeholder = e.g. Dirt, Stone
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.NoHarvest.ExceptBlockTags.placeholder = e.g. Soil
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.NoUse.ExceptBlocks.placeholder = e.g. Door_Wood, Chest
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.NoUse.ExceptBlockTags.placeholder = e.g. Door
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.NoDamage.Entities.placeholder = e.g. Player, Trork_Warrior
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.DamageMultiplier.Entities.placeholder = e.g. Player, Kweebec_Elder
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.ModifyRules.Active.tooltip = Whether the matched volumes enforce their Always Active rules. Off suspends the rules at runtime without changing the configured rule list.
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.ModifyRules.Operation.tooltip = What to do to the matched volumes' Always Active rules. Set adds or replaces the chosen rule, Append merges the rule's list fields into an existing rule of that type, Set Field sets a single chosen field on an existing rule (empty value clears just that field), Remove deletes the rule, and Set Rules Active toggles whether the rules are enforced.
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.ModifyRules.RuleField.tooltip = Which field of the chosen rule to set. Leave the value empty to clear just that field. Other fields of the rule are left unchanged.
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.ModifyRules.RuleType.tooltip = Which Always Active rule this effect targets. For Set Rules Active, leave on All Rules to toggle every rule at once, or pick a rule type to enable/disable just that one.
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.common.Enabled.tooltip = Whether this rule is enforced. Turn off to suspend just this rule while leaving the rest of the volume's rules active.
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.SendSignal.SignalKeys.tooltip = Comma-separated tag keys carried by the signal. Receivers match them with a Tag Condition (Source: Event / Signal), firing if any key matches. The signal also carries the triggering event's position, so receiver effects can fire there. Paired by position with Signal Values.
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.SendSignal.SignalValues.tooltip = Optional comma-separated value for each Signal Key, paired by position. A receiving Tag Condition matches only when its Tag Value also matches (blank matches any). Leave an entry blank to send that key with no value.
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.PlaceBlock.BlockState.tooltip = Optional block state to apply to the placed block. Leave this field blank to use the default state.
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.ReplaceBlockType.FromBlockState.tooltip = Optional state that the source blocks must have. Leave this field blank to use the default state.
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.ReplaceBlockType.ToBlockState.tooltip = Optional block state to apply to replacement blocks. Leave this field blank to use the default state.
triggerVolumeEffectEditor.field.ReplaceBlockType.Origin.tooltip = Where the AABB is anchored: the trigger volume origin, the triggering entity, where the event/signal happened, or an absolute world coordinate. Only applies to the AABB bounds mode. Shape always uses the volume.
